    "notes": "From a photo in Strat-O-Matic's WordPress media library (item 688588, uploaded 2026-09-10 with the photos for its 'WSBG FINAL: GENE ABOOD WORLD CHAMPION' announcement, sourceUrl; file at sourceImage): Adcock's advanced card on top of a stack, photographed rotated 90 degrees. It is a small phone photo (480x640) but the card fills most of it, lies flat and is in focus: after uprighting, every cell, glyph and d20 range is readable at 2.3-5x. Read twice: (1) from a 2.3x view of the whole uprighted card, (2) from 3.6x crops of each platoon grid and a 5x crop of RHP column 1; no differences. YEAR AND TEAM: the card prints neither, but the announcement's recap credits Gene Abood's 1957 Milwaukee team with 'Joe Adcock's two home runs' (the WSBG final used 1957 Milwaukee and 1979 Montreal for Abood), and the card fits Adcock's injury-shortened 1957 (209 AB, 12 HR, 51 SO in 65 games; see validator figures). Markers: diamond ◆, downTriangle ▼, upTriangle △ (LHP col3 roll3 and RHP col3 roll3, each with an italic 'SI* / lo (ss)' d20 split on the two lines directly beneath, before the next roll; binding unambiguous), omega Ω, '?' as questionMark, underlined class letters as 'underline:C'. 'plus injury' prints on its own line under 'strikeout' (col3 roll9 of both grids)."
